    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n96577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρ-ησις</span></b> , also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέρ-εσις</span></b>  (q.v.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>deprivation, loss</i>, of a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.63
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πνεύματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					865b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. αἰσθήσεως ὁ θάνατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					3p.60U.
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῆς ἀναπνοῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.795
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τοῦ ὀφθαλμοῦ,
			ὀφθαλμῶν</span>, i.e. blindness, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Judic.</u>
				42
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17(1).401
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
